# Madar Backend — environment template
# Copy to .env and adjust. Never commit the real .env.

# HTTP server
PORT=3000
HOST=0.0.0.0

# Where project workspaces live on the host (bind-mounted into containers)
WSD_PROJECTS_DIR=/workspaces

# Base image for project workspaces. Built from Dockerfile.workspace
# (Ubuntu 26.04 LTS + Node 24 LTS) as wsd/workspace:latest; docker-compose.yml
# sets this same value for the app container, so changing it here alone has no
# effect in a compose install. The image carries io.madar.workspace.toolchain.*
# OCI labels and /etc/madar/workspace-toolchain.json (declared vs actual
# Ubuntu/Node/npm, build id/time and checks); no Docker CLI is installed in it.
WSD_WORKSPACE_IMAGE=wsd/workspace:latest

# Optional — admin-only workspace image refresh controls. Stale days mark the
# image old compared with its builtAt stamp (default 30, clamped 1..365). Refresh
# timeout bounds the synchronous Docker build in ms (default 900000, floor
# 60000). The refresh rate ceiling defaults to WSD_RATE_UPDATE_APPLY_MAX; set
# this to give POST /api/workspace-image/refresh its own per-IP budget.
WSD_WORKSPACE_STALE_DAYS=30
WSD_WORKSPACE_REFRESH_TIMEOUT_MS=900000
# WSD_RATE_WORKSPACE_REFRESH_MAX=2

# ── Chatbot (Ollama Cloud) ────────────────────────────────────
# REQUIRED — chat panel only.
OLLAMA_API_KEY=
OLLAMA_HOST=https://ollama.com
WSD_CHAT_MODEL=qwen3:30b

# ── opencode web (native UI, Big Pickle via Zen) ──────────────
# REQUIRED — free Zen key from https://opencode.ai/auth (no credit card).
OPENCODE_API_KEY=
# Container port opencode web listens on, bound to 127.0.0.1 only. It is NOT
# published: reach opencode through the authenticated proxy below.
WSD_OPENCODE_PORT=4096

# Optional — opencode update channel. The backend integration is verified
# against major 1 (SUPPORTED_MAJORS = [1]); a positive safe integer overrides
# the allowed major, and a missing/junk value falls back to 1. Setting 2 opts
# into the 2.x update channel without adapting this facade, so leave it at 1
# unless the backend supports that major.
WSD_UPDATE_OPENCODE_MAJOR=1

# ── Web IDE (single shared code-server, loopback-only) ───────
# Container port code-server listens on, bound to 127.0.0.1 only. NOT published.
# Code-only knob: docker-compose.yml hard-codes the internal 8080, so only a
# non-compose run ever moves it (matching the code-server port in entrypoint.sh).
WSD_IDE_INTERNAL_PORT=8080
# 8100 is NO LONGER PUBLISHED — kept solely so the port stays reserved and a
# project container can never claim the old IDE port. Setting it does not move
# the IDE; the dashboard is reachable through the proxy below.
WSD_IDE_PORT=8100

# ── Embedded-surface proxy (the ONLY route to the two above) ─
# Host port the authenticated proxy is published on. Requires an editor-or-above
# Madar session; proxies HTTP and websockets to code-server (under /ide) and
# opencode (at the origin root).
# PRODUCTION DEPLOYMENT: terminate TLS in front of BOTH this port and 3000. The
# TLS override binds the app container to 127.0.0.1 and nginx owns the public
# ports; on cleartext one on-path attacker reads the dashboard JWT (:3000) and
# the madar_embed cookie (:4097) alike. See docs/INSTALL.md ("Security in
# production deployment") for the nginx/TLS setup.
# WSD_EMBED_PROXY_PORT=4097

# ── Reverse proxy in front of the app ────────────────────────
# Comma-separated IPs/CIDRs (or aliases) of proxies allowed to set
# X-Forwarded-For / X-Forwarded-Proto. In production the TLS overlay sets
# "loopback,uniquelocal": nginx on 127.0.0.1 plus the Docker bridge gateway.
# Per-IP rate limiters then see the real client, and a trusted hop's
# X-Forwarded-Proto: https is what makes the embed cookie carry `Secure`.
# Wildcard CIDRs ending in /0 are refused. Do not set this in the base .env —
# the base compose publishes 0.0.0.0, where a spoofed header would defeat every
# limiter; the TLS overlay owns the explicit list after loopback-only binds are
# verified. WSD_TRUST_PROXY=1|true is a deprecated alias, accepted only when
# WSD_TRUSTED_PROXIES is absent.
# WSD_TRUSTED_PROXIES=loopback,uniquelocal

# ── Session signing secret ────────────────────────────────────
# Optional: leave it empty and the app generates a random secret once and keeps
# it at $WSD_DATA_DIR/jwt.secret (0600), so sessions are unforgeable and survive
# restarts. A blank, known-weak or under-32-character value is refused outright
# — there is deliberately no default to share. It signs sessions only; it is
# never used as the current provider-encryption key.
#   node -e "console.log(require('crypto').randomBytes(32).toString('hex'))"
# JWT_SECRET=

# ── At-rest encryption of provider API keys ──────────────────
# Optional master key for current `v2:` AES-256-GCM blobs. When empty the app
# generates a random 32-byte key and keeps it at $WSD_DATA_DIR/enc.key (0600).
# Rotating or losing this value makes current stored provider keys undecryptable
# — re-enter them from the Providers page.
# WSD_ENC_KEY=
#
# Legacy `enc1:` blobs are migration-only: they are decrypted with the old
# WSD_ENCRYPTION_KEY (or previous signing secret) plus $WSD_DATA_DIR/crypto.salt
# and re-sealed as `v2:` when the provider store is loaded or rewritten. Keep
# crypto.salt only while legacy values remain.

# ── Network ──────────────────────────────────────────────────
# If empty, the first non-internal IPv4 is detected automatically.
# WSD_PUBLIC_IP=192.168.0.110

# ── Production TLS deployment (single app instance) ──────────
# See docs/INSTALL.md for the full sequence: nginx + certbot on the host, the
# prod compose override binding 3000/4097 to 127.0.0.1, and the binding guard.
# MADAR_DOMAIN=madar.example.com
# WSD_TESTING=0
